      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, from the bug and the failing tests, I think maybe the correct way to address this is instead of producing a validation error when we try to create a default view of of a texture, we construct the view with only the public usages.\n\nSo w.r.t to the bug, this means that we probably don\u0027t need to change the validation logic, just the construction logic for the view?\n\nThis also begs the question as to whether the `DawnTextureInternalUsageDescriptor` should be a valid chain on `TextureViewDescriptor` on top of just `TextureDescriptor`. That way in situations where a Dawn power user is doing something with textures/views that require the internal usages, they can do it by explicitly chaining the additional descriptor when constructing the view.",
      "revId": "b36519b9e8128c83781966cdecd04d20543fe266",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
